{\\pi }{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534788 true] [17592186310291 1000 #edb/ref 17592186310292 13194139534788 true] [17592186310291 1000 #edb/ref 17592186310293 13194139534788 true] [17592186310291 1000 #edb/ref 17592186310294 13194139534788 true] [17592186310291 1000 #edb/ref 17592186310295 13194139534788 true] [17592186310291 1000 #edb/ref 17592186310296 13194139534788 true] [17592186310291 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534788 true] [17592186310291 1041 "selection" 13194139534788 true] [17592186310291 1104 #edb/ref 17592186310293 13194139534788 true] [17592186310291 1110 #uuid "4446dbf4-8054-58a4-b632-598eaf9f4443" 13194139534788 true] [17592186310292 1034 "\\frac{2\\pi }{3}" 13194139534788 true] [17592186310292 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534788 true] [17592186310292 1111 #uuid "eab8e23c-f8ac-5849-baee-03938fa4522d" 13194139534788 true] [17592186310293 1034 "\\frac{\\pi }{2}" 13194139534788 true] [17592186310293 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534788 true] [17592186310293 1111 #uuid "0062029e-fe63-5b21-bc66-8a1fa62fa9a2" 13194139534788 true] [17592186310294 1034 "\\frac{\\pi }{4}" 13194139534788 true] [17592186310294 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534788 true] [17592186310294 1111 #uuid "1f740ded-2b09-5901-81a5-0ce42c8c0d14" 13194139534788 true] [17592186310295 1034 "\\pi " 13194139534788 true] [17592186310295 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534788 true] [17592186310295 1111 #uuid "93f6f09a-c6c4-5cf4-a922-314dd0599adb" 13194139534788 true] [17592186310296 1034 "2\\pi " 13194139534788 true] [17592186310296 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534788 true] [17592186310296 1111 #uuid "10561597-0e6f-54cc-92c3-cc7662d0f3dc" 13194139534788 true] [17592186310297 1017 #edb/ref 17592186310298 13194139534788 true] [17592186310297 1089 "q-81375" 13194139534788 true] [17592186310297 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139534788 true] [17592186310297 1100 "Consider the function $f(x)=2x{e}^{-{x}^{2}}.$ Which of the following statements are true?\n\n- ${\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }f(x)\\,\\text{d}x$ is convergent\n- ${\\int }_{-\\infty }^{0}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x$ is divergent\n- ${\\int }_{-\\infty }^{\\infty }f(x)\\,\\text{d}x$ is divergent" 13194139534788 true] [17592186310297 1113 #uuid "7604850e-71a3-5707-ae7f-3270a2b4ae23" 13194139534788 true] [17592186310297 1145 "Suppose we have an improper integral in which both the left and right endpoints are unbounded:\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{-\\infty }^{\\infty }f(x)\\,\\text{d}x\n$$\n\nIf the integrand $f(x)$ is continuous on $(-\\infty ,\\infty ),$ then we can break the integral up into two improper integrals, each with a single unbounded endpoint:\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{-\\infty }^{\\infty }f(x)\\,\\text{d}x={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{0}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }f(x)\\,\\text{d}x\n$$\n\nThen, we can compute each of the two integrals separately and combine their results. \n\n**Watch out!** If either of the two integrals on the right-hand side is divergent, then the integral on the left-hand side is also divergent.\n\nFirst, we calculate the antiderivative using a substitution.  Let $u={x}^{2}$,  then $\\text{d}u=2x\\,\\text{d}x.$ Hence, the antiderivative is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int 2x{e}^{-{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int {e}^{-u}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =-{e}^{-u}+C \\\\  & =-{e}^{-{x}^{2}}+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, let's evaluate each integral in turn.\n\n- Statement I is true. Computing the required integral, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }2x{e}^{-{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x & ={lim}_{a\\to \\infty }{\\int }_{0}^{a}2x{e}^{-{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={lim}_{a\\to \\infty }({-{e}^{-{x}^{2}}|}_{0}^{a}) \\\\  & ={lim}_{a\\to \\infty }(-{e}^{-{a}^{2}}+{e}^{0}) \\\\  & =0+1 \\\\  & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo the integral converges.\n\n- Statement II is false. Computing the required integral, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-\\infty }^{0}2x{e}^{-{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x & ={lim}_{a\\to -\\infty }{\\int }_{a}^{0}2x{e}^{-{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={lim}_{a\\to -\\infty }({-{e}^{-{x}^{2}}|}_{a}^{0}) \\\\  & ={lim}_{a\\to -\\infty }(-{e}^{0}+{e}^{-{a}^{2}}) \\\\  & =-1+0 \\\\  & =-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo the integral converges.\n\n- Statement III is false. The integral in statement III can be expressed as\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{-\\infty }^{\\infty }f(x)\\,\\text{d}x={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{0}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=1-1=0.\n$$\n\nSo the integral converges.\n\nIn conclusion, only statement I is true." 13194139534788 true] [17592186310298 1000 #edb/ref 17592186310299 13194139534788 true] [17592186310298 1000 #edb/ref 17592186310300 13194139534788 true] [17592186310298 1000 #edb/ref 17592186310301 13194139534788 true] [17592186310298 1000 #edb/ref 17592186310302 13194139534788 true] [17592186310298 1000 #edb/ref 17592186310303 13194139534788 true] [17592186310298 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534788 true] [17592186310298 1041 "selection" 13194139534788 true] [17592186310298 1104 #edb/ref 17592186310301 13194139534788 true] [17592186310298 1110 #uuid "bf9aa03e-61e1-53a8-a84b-78ad52987fc4" 13194139534788 true] [17592186310299 1034 "I, II, and III" 13194139534788 true] [17592186310299 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534788 true] [17592186310299 1111 #uuid "b367d6b8-dc48-53e1-b99a-059c738fc142" 13194139534788 true] [17592186310300 1034 "I and III only" 13194139534788 true] [17592186310300 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534788 true] [17592186310300 1111 #uuid "5e647f77-36e2-568a-9f6e-2c4a7292ebe4" 13194139534788 true] [17592186310301 1034 "I only" 13194139534788 true] [17592186310301 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534788 true] [17592186310301 1111 #uuid "a8cb1c9a-e1b9-56dc-920d-a0ae428af52a" 13194139534788 true] [17592186310302 1034 "III only" 13194139534788 true] [17592186310302 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534788 true] [17592186310302 1111 #uuid "c39062a7-ba40-5f22-88b6-544afff931b0" 13194139534788 true] [17592186310303 1034 "I and II only" 1319413953478